\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {4.4}{\ignorespaces Transfer from byte-level pretraining to decision accuracy at a matched budget: 2,000 training rows, 500 test rows, six nominal epochs, identical order, steps, batch, optimiser, learning rate and training seed. Banking77 is the class-balanced 77-way draw (three seeds, 500 test rows each); AG News is the class-balanced four-way draw (three seeds, 500 unique test rows, 1,500 pooled decisions). The AG interval is the paired crossed-seed/item bootstrap and crosses zero; the Banking77 8,000-row arm in Table\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {tab:rows} is a different, row-scaling experiment and is not this matched contrast. The per-seed AG rows are the same six cells, shown so the pooled interval cannot hide a sign change. Generated from \texttt  {results/transfer/*.json} and the recovered six-cell summary.\relax }}{19}{table.caption.14}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:transfer}{{4.4}{19}{Transfer from byte-level pretraining to decision accuracy at a matched budget: 2,000 training rows, 500 test rows, six nominal epochs, identical order, steps, batch, optimiser, learning rate and training seed. Banking77 is the class-balanced 77-way draw (three seeds, 500 test rows each); AG News is the class-balanced four-way draw (three seeds, 500 unique test rows, 1,500 pooled decisions). The AG interval is the paired crossed-seed/item bootstrap and crosses zero; the Banking77 8,000-row arm in Table~\ref {tab:rows} is a different, row-scaling experiment and is not this matched contrast. The per-seed AG rows are the same six cells, shown so the pooled interval cannot hide a sign change. Generated from \texttt {results/transfer/*.json} and the recovered six-cell summary.\relax }{table.caption.14}{}}
