\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {4.7}{\ignorespaces Scaling at matched tokens per parameter ($D/N = 10$) on the 1{,}633{,}580{,}647-token corpus. \emph  {Exhaustive} is the non-overlapping full held-out pass (9{,}967{,}360 scored bytes); \emph  {sampled} is 64 windows of 1{,}024 bytes at mask seed 1234, the configuration every rung was scored with. The large rung has only the sampled score: its exhaustive pass was not run, so no exhaustive value is extrapolated for it. The fitted exponents are least squares on $\qopname  \relax o{log}\mathrm  {bpb}$ against $\qopname  \relax o{log}N$, over the rungs that carry each protocol. The 256-byte context of the tiny rung bounds the sequence it was trained on, not the number of parameters it has.\relax }}{26}{table.caption.17}\protected@file@percent }
