\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5.1}{\ignorespaces Decode versus score with everything else fixed: same encoder, same initialisation, same rows in the same order, same steps, batch, learning rate and seed. \emph  {Score} evaluates every candidate in one pass and cannot emit an out-of-bank label; \emph  {decode} fills the label's byte slots iteratively and is matched against the bank, so it can. Latency is batch-1 wall clock on CPU over the same test rows, and therefore a lower bound on what an autoregressive decoder of the same label length would cost. GPU seconds per 1,000 decisions come from $1000\times p_{50}$ and are CPU seconds here, so they overstate an accelerator. The last column is the GPU rate at which 1,000 local decisions cost what Jev charges for that task's billed payload at \$0.042/MTok; it is rate-free because no price for this machine is recorded anywhere in the repository. Read from \texttt  {results/decode\_vs\_score/*.json}.\relax }}{34}{table.caption.22}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:comparator}{{5.1}{34}{Decode versus score with everything else fixed: same encoder, same initialisation, same rows in the same order, same steps, batch, learning rate and seed. \emph {Score} evaluates every candidate in one pass and cannot emit an out-of-bank label; \emph {decode} fills the label's byte slots iteratively and is matched against the bank, so it can. Latency is batch-1 wall clock on CPU over the same test rows, and therefore a lower bound on what an autoregressive decoder of the same label length would cost. GPU seconds per 1,000 decisions come from $1000\times p_{50}$ and are CPU seconds here, so they overstate an accelerator. The last column is the GPU rate at which 1,000 local decisions cost what Jev charges for that task's billed payload at \$0.042/MTok; it is rate-free because no price for this machine is recorded anywhere in the repository. Read from \texttt {results/decode\_vs\_score/*.json}.\relax }{table.caption.22}{}}
\newlabel{tab:comparator@cref}{{[table][1][5]5.1}{[1][34][]34}}
