\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.1}{\ignorespaces Per-class Banking77 error concentration for the native query head. Left: Lorenz curve of the 338{} errors, with Jev's 234{} errors beside it. Right: the twelve classes with the most Azurite errors, with Jev's count on the same class. The largest single class, \texttt  {pending\_transfer}, accounts for 12{} of the 338{} errors; 70{} of 77 classes have at least one. The boundary is broad, not concentrated in a few intents. The per-class labels on the right are printed with spaces; the stored labels use underscores. Values are recomputed from the per-example records by \texttt  {thesis/gen\_figures.py}.\relax }}{40}{figure.caption.27}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:error-concentration}{{5.1}{40}{Per-class Banking77 error concentration for the native query head. Left: Lorenz curve of the \FigErrorTotal {} errors, with Jev's \FigErrorJevTotal {} errors beside it. Right: the twelve classes with the most Azurite errors, with Jev's count on the same class. The largest single class, \FigErrorTopClass , accounts for \FigErrorTopClassCount {} of the \FigErrorTotal {} errors; \FigErrorClassesWithError {} of 77 classes have at least one. The boundary is broad, not concentrated in a few intents. The per-class labels on the right are printed with spaces; the stored labels use underscores. Values are recomputed from the per-example records by \texttt {thesis/gen\_figures.py}.\relax }{figure.caption.27}{}}
\newlabel{fig:error-concentration@cref}{{[figure][1][5]5.1}{[1][39][]40}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5.4}{\ignorespaces The message-query head on all 3{,}080 official Banking77 rows, with the exact 24 public Jev examples per row and the same gold/Jev vector as the matched test. ``Examples'' is the mean number of complete lines that fit in the 1{,}020-byte context budget. The old head is the E4 mean-pool head; the query head replaces mean pooling with a masked attention pool queried by the customer message. \texttt  {old\_a2c} is the head control under the same packing; \texttt  {query\_a0} is the example control. The P0 bar is Jev's 92.40\%. Wilson intervals are 95\%; McNemar is exact and two-sided; the bootstrap lower bound is the 5th percentile of 10{,}000 paired resamples, seed 0. Read from \texttt  {results/jev\_query/eval/summary.json}.\relax }}{41}{table.caption.28}\protected@file@percent }
