\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.3}{\ignorespaces Query-head accuracy against mean context length. The three points are message-only (0 examples), the native complete-example packing (11.9{} examples on average), and the joint 5{,}120-byte fine-tune (24 examples). The dashed line is Jev's 92.40\%; the diamond marks the reconstructed median Jev prompt, 10{,}683{} bytes, of which 7{,}801{} bytes are the 77 category definitions. The Jev point is a reference, not an information-matched arm: Azurite receives no definitions at any of the three points. Values are recomputed from the stored summaries and per-example files by \texttt  {thesis/gen\_figures.py}.\relax }}{44}{figure.caption.31}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:budget}{{5.3}{44}{Query-head accuracy against mean context length. The three points are message-only (0 examples), the native complete-example packing (\QueryEff {} examples on average), and the joint 5{,}120-byte fine-tune (24 examples). The dashed line is Jev's \QueryJevPct \%; the diamond marks the reconstructed median Jev prompt, \FigJevPromptMedian {} bytes, of which \FigJevDefinitionsBytes {} bytes are the 77 category definitions. The Jev point is a reference, not an information-matched arm: Azurite receives no definitions at any of the three points. Values are recomputed from the stored summaries and per-example files by \texttt {thesis/gen\_figures.py}.\relax }{figure.caption.31}{}}
